# vdbvisualizetree

- Label: VDB Visualize Tree
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 7 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbvisualizetree.html
- Summary (EN): Builds a geometry visualizing the topology of a VDB, showing which regions are active, since a VDB is only defined where it has been activated. Output is geometry.
- Résumé (FR) : Dessine la topologie d'un VDB (feuilles, nœuds internes et tuiles actives) pour voir quelles régions sont réellement activées.

- Inputs meaning: ["src: a Float, Vector or Integer VDB whose topology is converted into a tree"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the VDB type the source accepts", "Leaf Nodes: drawn in blue, as wireframe or solid boxes", "Internal Nodes: non-leaf nodes as wireframe or solid boxes; first internal level green, others orange", "Active Tiles: active nodes holding the default empty value; positive values red, negative values white", "Points: described as one point at the centre of each node, but the section lists Wireframe Boxes and Solid Boxes as its options"]

- Caveats: ["The Points section lists Wireframe Boxes and Solid Boxes, which does not match its description of single points; the page does not explain this, so check the output in Houdini"]

